      "writtenOn": "2021-06-30T18:45:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, the underlying networks can always be updated; they\u0027re done through a NetworkAgent.setUnderlyingNetworks() call, and then updated in the NAI\u0027s declaredUnderlyingNetworks (see handling for \"case NetworkAgent.EVENT_UNDERLYING_NETWORKS_CHANGED\")\n\nThis change here is made so we can use the nai.shouldApplyUnderlyingTransports() below, instead of increasing the number of parameters that are encapsulated by the NAI. It\u0027s functionally a no-op change by passing a NAI instead of capabilities and underlying networks separately.",
      "parentUuid": "69eed167_c986a854",
